              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 21-year-old female patient, admitted on 09/02/2021 with acute lower abdominal pain and a positive pregnancy test. Clinical examination and transvaginal ultrasound confirmed a right-sided tubal ectopic pregnancy without signs of rupture. Serum beta-hCG levels were markedly elevated. Given the clinical presentation and patient's hemodynamic stability, a laparoscopic approach was chosen. The patient underwent laparoscopic salpingectomy of the right fallopian tube with successful removal of the ectopic pregnancy. The postoperative course was uneventful. Analgesic medication was administered as needed. The patient was counseled regarding the implications for future fertility and contraception. Discharge occurred on 11/02/2021 in good general condition. Please arrange follow-up including repeat beta-hCG measurement. Kind regards.</div>"
            },
